{"id":"code-topo-order","title":"Smallest topological order","category":"code","difficulty":3,"prompt":"Write a Python function `topo_order(n: int, edges: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[int]`. The nodes are 0 to n-1 and an edge `(a, b)` means a must come before b. Return the lexicographically smallest ordering of all nodes that respects every edge, or an empty list if the graph has a cycle. Edges may repeat.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"topo_order","tests":["assert topo_order(0, []) == []","assert topo_order(3, []) == [0, 1, 2]","assert topo_order(4, [(1, 0), (2, 0), (3, 1)]) == [2, 3, 1, 0]","assert topo_order(3, [(0, 1), (1, 2), (2, 0)]) == []","assert topo_order(5, [(4, 0), (4, 1), (3, 1), (2, 3)]) == [2, 3, 4, 0, 1]","assert topo_order(2, [(0, 1), (0, 1)]) == [0, 1]","assert topo_order(2, [(1, 1)]) == []","assert topo_order(6, [(5, 0), (5, 2), (4, 0), (4, 1), (2, 3), (3, 1)]) == [4, 5, 0, 2, 3, 1]"]},"reference":"```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef topo_order(n: int, edges: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[int]:\n    followers = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    indegree = [0] * n\n    for a, b in edges:\n        followers[a].append(b)\n        indegree[b] += 1\n    ready = [node for node in range(n) if indegree[node] == 0]\n    heapq.heapify(ready)\n    order = []\n    while ready:\n        node = heapq.heappop(ready)\n        order.append(node)\n        for nxt in followers[node]:\n            indegree[nxt] -= 1\n            if indegree[nxt] == 0:\n                heapq.heappush(ready, nxt)\n    return order if len(order) == n else []\n```","answers":["```python\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef topo_order(n: int, edges: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[int]:\n    followers = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    indegree = [0] * n\n    for a, b in edges:\n        followers[a].append(b)\n        indegree[b] += 1\n    ready = deque(node for node in range(n) if indegree[node] == 0)\n    order = []\n    while ready:\n        node = ready.popleft()\n        order.append(node)\n        for nxt in followers[node]:\n            indegree[nxt] -= 1\n            if indegree[nxt] == 0:\n                ready.append(nxt)\n    return order if len(order) == n else []\n```","```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef topo_order(n: int, edges: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[int]:\n    followers = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    indegree = [0] * n\n    for a, b in edges:\n        followers[a].append(b)\n        indegree[b] += 1\n    ready = [node for node in range(n) if indegree[node] == 0]\n    heapq.heapify(ready)\n    order = []\n    while ready:\n        node = heapq.heappop(ready)\n        order.append(node)\n        for nxt in followers[node]:\n            indegree[nxt] -= 1\n            if indegree[nxt] == 0:\n                heapq.heappush(ready, nxt)\n    return order if len(order) == n else []\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.875,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":7,"total":8,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.152,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":168,"output_tokens":256,"cost_usd":0.0001448,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":1.0,"passed":true,"answer":1,"details":{"passed":8,"total":8,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.152,"answer":"reference"}},"input_tokens":168,"output_tokens":278,"cost_usd":0.0001558,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":2,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.875,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":7,"total":8,"tests":